{"": "This clause differs from standard practice because it makes the tenant responsible for all repairs, including major fixes such as walls or roof, whereas Indian rental law typically requires the landlord to handle those major repairs and limits the tenant to minor upkeep like cleaning or changing light bulbs.

This provision exceeds the legal limit set by the Model Tenancy Act Sections 13(1) and 15(2), which assign only day‑to‑day maintenance to the tenant.

Because of this mismatch, a tenant could face unexpected repair bills and potential disputes, while the landlord may be relieved of obligations that the law intends to keep on them."}
